id: ops-windows-runtime-cleanup
title: Investigate EPERM during Windows release runtime fixture cleanup
description: "The Node 26 windows-consumers job for PR #295 at c1e0c80 failed in Native Windows locked release runtime. Actions run 44419424002, job 135208153618. The same check passed at 959f9ab and the runtime implementation and fixture are byte-identical across the two heads."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:release",ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-ops#295",windows
created_at: "2026-11-18T23:23:22.255Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T23:36:58.026Z"
author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: Determine why the fixture directory remains locked at cleanup and demonstrate reliable cleanup with the linked native Windows test command while retaining its install assertions.
severity: medium
environment: "Native Windows CI, Node 26.13.1"
repro_steps: Run the linked command on native Windows with Node 26.13.1. The CI observation occurred in the fixture named runtime installs only locked production dependencies without lifecycle scripts.
expected_result: The test asserts the locked installation contract and cleans up its temporary directory.
actual_result: "Recursive rmSync in the fixture finally block at test/release-runtime.test.ts:81 returned EPERM and failed the check."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-18T23:30:45.549Z",codex-sol,Round CX is checking the existing Node 26 rerun and the exact fixture cleanup. The native locked-runtime step passed on attempt 2. The original failure was recursive cleanup after the install assertions.
  "2026-11-18T23:34:21.411Z",codex-sol,"Attempt 1 of run 44419424002 failed with EPERM at test/release-runtime.test.ts:81 on Node 26. The existing attempt 2, job 135212982749, passed the native locked runtime step and the complete Windows job on the same head. The two runtime files also passed 8 of 8 tests on Linux Node 26.13.0. With no reproduced cleanup failure, the fixture is unchanged."
  "2026-11-18T23:36:54.917Z",codex-sol,The Windows investigation is recorded with the Round CX context fix in commit 3e0a9a8. The successful same-head rerun leaves a single observed cleanup failure and no reproduced Windows regression. Keep the item available if cleanup fails again.
files[2]{path,scope}:
  test/release-runtime-windows.test.ts,project
  test/release-runtime.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-runtime.test.ts test/release-runtime-windows.test.ts,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-18T23:23:25.129Z",local_mutation,followup/windows-release-runtime-cleanup
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/ci-tiers.md,project,Native Windows release runtime gate
body: ""
